  "interpretation": "The paper's '86% agreement' claim refers to per-feature Spearman rho between individual text features and LLM-judge annotations, not to agreement at the ConstraintState (5-dimension) level. Only 3 of 8 features have reported judge validation: ei_logic_density (rho=0.93), eii_bigram_repetition (rho=0.98), eiii_proper_case_ratio (rho=0.92) -- mean of validated features = 0.943. The 5 unvalidated features (ei_syntax_cv, eii_filler_ratio, eii_unique_word_ratio, eii_truncation_ratio, eiii_number_integrity) have no reported judge correlation. The 86% figure likely averages the 3 validated rhos (0.94) with assumed correlations of ~0.80-0.83 for unvalidated features, or it may include additional unreported measurements. It is NOT a measure of agreement between the Hybrid extractor's 5D ConstraintState output and any independent criterion -- it is a feature-level validation claim covering only 3/8 features with documented evidence."
